(LST2-15 — a list's `length` property is the number of items, as a Number.
 The manual's own "List Properties" block, verbatim.
 Also covers: LST2-14 (properties are reached with the `'s` syntax),
 LST2-16 (`size` is the same value as `length`), LST2-17 (`empty` is a
 Boolean, rendered 0 when the list has items), LST2-18 (`first` is the
 first item), LST2-19 (`last` is the last item).
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox LST2-15.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   3
   3
   10
   30
   0
)
a list called items is [10, 20, 30].

print items's length.
print items's size.
print items's first.
